IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 10, Instruments not covered by the
-- Legislation Act 2003, and parliamentary resolutions (ss 46 to 47), and PART 11,
-- Regulations (s 51). Legislative instruments and notifiable instruments are covered by
-- the Legislation Act 2003, which is NOT in this text: where this Act points there, the
-- answer is NOTHING (the text does not give it), never a guess.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.

§ `Part 10: Instruments not covered by the Legislation Act 2003, and parliamentary resolutions`

§§ `Section 46(1): this Act applies to an instrument made under a power`

-- src:882 | 46 Construction of instruments
-- src:883 | (1) If a provision confers on a person (the authority) the power to make an instrument other than a legislative instrument, notifiable instrument or a rule of court, then:
-- src:884 | (a) this Act applies to any instrument so made as if it were an Act and as if each provision of the instrument were a section of an Act; and
-- src:885 | (b) expressions used in any instrument so made have the same meaning as in the Act or instrument, as in force from time to time, that authorises the making of the instrument in which the expressions are used; and
-- src:886 | (c) any instrument so made is to be read and construed subject to the enabling legislation as in force from time to time, and so as not to exceed the power of the authority.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 46(1) (src:882-886)
GIVEN `a provision confers on a person the power to make an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act applies to the instrument as if it were an Act and each of its provisions a section of an Act` `a provision confers on a person the power to make an instrument` `the instrument is a legislative instrument` `the instrument is a notifiable instrument` `the instrument is a rule of court` MEANS
        `a provision confers on a person the power to make an instrument`
    AND (NOT `the instrument is a legislative instrument`)
    AND (NOT `the instrument is a notifiable instrument`)
    AND (NOT `the instrument is a rule of court`)

§§ `Section 46(2): valid to the extent it is within the power`

-- src:887 | (2) If any instrument so made would, but for this subsection, be construed as being in excess of the authority’s power, it is to be taken to be a valid instrument to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 46(2) (src:887)
GIVEN `the instrument is one to which section 46(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this part of the instrument is within the authority's power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this part of the instrument is valid` `the instrument is one to which section 46(1) applies` `this part of the instrument is within the authority's power` MEANS
    IF   `the instrument is one to which section 46(1) applies`
    THEN JUST `this part of the instrument is within the authority's power`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 46(3): amendment of an instrument by an Act`

-- The Note to s 46 says a parallel exists for legislative and notifiable instruments in
-- section 13 of the Legislation Act 2003; that Act is not in this text, so for those the
-- answer here is NOTHING.
-- src:888 | (3) The amendment of an instrument, other than a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument, or a rule of court, by an Act does not prevent the instrument, as so amended, from being amended or repealed by the authority.
-- src:889 | Note: This provision has a parallel, in relation to legislative instruments and notifiable instruments, in section 13 of the Legislation Act 2003.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 46(3) (src:888-889)
GIVEN `the instrument is a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an amendment of the instrument by an Act prevents the authority from later amending or repealing it` `the instrument is a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court` MEANS
    IF   `the instrument is a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 46AA: prescribing matters by reference to other instruments`

DECLARE `Matter incorporated` IS ONE OF
    `the provisions of an Act`
    `the provisions of a legislative instrument that is disallowable within the meaning of the Legislation Act 2003`
    `the provisions of a legislative instrument that was disallowable under this or any other Act at some time before 1 January 2005`
    `the provisions of rules of court`
    `a matter contained in any other instrument or writing`

DECLARE `Time at which the matter is taken` IS ONE OF
    `as in force at a particular time`
    `as in force from time to time`
    `as in force or existing when the instrument commences`
    `as in force or existing at a time before the instrument commences`

-- 46AA(1)(a): the listed matters may be applied, adopted or incorporated as in force at a
-- particular time or as in force from time to time. 46AA(1)(b) and (2): any other instrument
-- or writing only as in force or existing when the instrument commences or at an earlier time,
-- and NOT from time to time. 46AA(4): the section does not apply to a form, so for a form
-- the answer here is NOTHING.
-- src:890 | 46AA Prescribing matters by reference to other instruments
-- src:891 | (1) If legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in relation to any matter in an instrument, other than a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court, that instrument may make provision in relation to that matter:
-- src:892 | (a) by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any of the following, as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time:
-- src:893 | (i) the provisions of an Act;
-- src:894 | (ii) the provisions of a legislative instrument covered by subsection (3);
-- src:895 | (iii) the provisions of rules of court; or
-- src:896 | (b) subject to subsection (2), by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained in any other instrument or writing as in force or existing at:
-- src:897 | (i) the time the first-mentioned instrument commences; or
-- src:898 | (ii) a time before the first-mentioned instrument commences (whether or not the other instrument is still in force, or the other writing still exists, at the time the first-mentioned instrument commences).
-- src:899 | (2) The instrument may not make provision in relation to that matter by applying, adopting or incorporating any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time.
-- src:900 | (3) The following legislative instruments are covered by this subsection:
-- src:901 | (a) disallowable legislative instruments within the meaning of the Legislation Act 2003;
-- src:902 | (b) legislative instruments that were disallowable under this or any other Act at any time before 1 January 2005.
-- src:903 | Note 1: Section 4 of the Legislation Act 2003 defines a disallowable legislative instrument as a legislative instrument to which section 42 of that Act applies.
-- src:904 | Note 2: The substantive provisions of the Legislation Act 2003 commenced on 1 January 2005.
-- src:905 | Forms
-- src:906 | (4) If an instrument provides for a form to be used, this section does not apply in relation to the form.
-- src:907 | Note: This provision has a parallel, in relation to legislative instruments and notifiable instruments, in section 14 of the Legislation Act 2003.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 46AA (src:890-907)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter incorporated`
      timing IS A `Time at which the matter is taken`
      `the authorising legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in an instrument that is not a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter concerns a form to be used under the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the instrument may apply, adopt or incorporate the matter at this time` matter timing `the authorising legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in an instrument that is not a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court` `the matter concerns a form to be used under the instrument` MEANS
    IF   `the matter concerns a form to be used under the instrument`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   NOT `the authorising legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in an instrument that is not a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST ((NOT fromTimeToTime) OR mayBeTakenFromTimeToTime)
    WHERE
        fromTimeToTime MEANS timing EQUALS `as in force from time to time`
        mayBeTakenFromTimeToTime MEANS
            CONSIDER matter
            WHEN `the provisions of an Act` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the provisions of a legislative instrument that is disallowable within the meaning of the Legislation Act 2003` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the provisions of a legislative instrument that was disallowable under this or any other Act at some time before 1 January 2005` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the provisions of rules of court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a matter contained in any other instrument or writing` THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 47: construction of resolutions`

-- src:908 | 47 Construction of resolutions
-- src:909 | Where any resolution is or has been passed by either House of the Parliament in purported pursuance of any Act, then the resolution shall be read and construed subject to the Constitution and to the Act under which it purports to have been passed, to the intent that where the resolution would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of authority, it shall nevertheless be a valid resolution to the extent to which it is not in excess of authority.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 47 (src:908-909)
GIVEN `a House of the Parliament passed the resolution in purported pursuance of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this part of the resolution is within the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this part of the resolution is valid` `a House of the Parliament passed the resolution in purported pursuance of an Act` `this part of the resolution is within the authority` MEANS
    IF   `a House of the Parliament passed the resolution in purported pursuance of an Act`
    THEN JUST `this part of the resolution is within the authority`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 11: Regulations`

§§ `Section 51: regulations`

-- src:910 | Part 11 — Regulations
-- src:911 | 51 Regulations
-- src:912 | The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:
-- src:913 | (a) required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed; or
-- src:914 | (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 51 (src:910-914)
GIVEN `the matter is required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor-General may make regulations prescribing the matter` `the matter is required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed` `the matter is necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act` MEANS
    `the matter is required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed`
    OR `the matter is necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act`
